# Module: Identity & Authentication

## Scope

User registration, login, JWT/refresh tokens, password reset, invitations, session management.

## Key Entities

`User`, `UserProfile`, `RefreshToken`, `LoginAttempt`, `UserInvitation`, `PasswordResetToken`

## Permissions

```
auth.profile.read
auth.profile.update
auth.password.change
users.invite
users.manage
```

## Commands & queries (MVP) — folder paths

| Type | Path under `SchoolSaaS.Application` |
|------|-------------------------------------|
| Login | `Commands/Auth/Login/` |
| Logout | `Commands/Auth/Logout/` |
| RefreshToken | `Commands/Auth/RefreshToken/` |
| Register | `Commands/Auth/Register/` |
| ForgotPassword | `Commands/Auth/ForgotPassword/` |
| ResetPassword | `Commands/Auth/ResetPassword/` |
| ChangePassword | `Commands/Auth/ChangePassword/` |
| AcceptInvitation | `Commands/Auth/AcceptInvitation/` |
| InviteUser | `Commands/Users/InviteUser/` |
| GetCurrentUser | `Queries/Auth/GetCurrentUser/` |

## Security Rules

- Passwords: bcrypt/Argon2, never log or return in responses
- JWT claims: `sub`, `tenant_id`, `email`, `roles[]`
- Refresh token rotation: invalidate old token on refresh
- Lockout after 5 failed attempts (Redis counter, 15-min lock)
- Reset tokens: single-use, 1-hour expiry

## Events

- `UserRegisteredIntegrationEvent`
- `PasswordResetRequestedIntegrationEvent`
- `UserLockedIntegrationEvent`

## API Prefix

`/api/v1/auth/*` and `/api/v1/users/*`

## Do NOT

- Store plaintext passwords or reset tokens
- Include sensitive claims in JWT beyond what's needed
- Allow login without tenant context resolution
